Rule 1 (tensor shapes should be the same)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 3 (first dimension of a tensor matches second dimension of the other)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 1)
>>
Rule 4 (primitive type variable should not be zero)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≠ 0
>>
Rule 5 (Integer indices only valid with int-compatible dtype)
{v_1 : tuple(int), v_2 : dtype} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] ≥ 0 ∧ v_2 = 1 ∨ v_2 = 2 ∨ v_2 = 3 ∨ v_2 = 4 ∨ v_2 = 5
